        "topic": "TypeScript",
        "question": "What are the benefits of using TypeScript in large-scale applications?",
        "answer": "TypeScript improves maintainability, scalability, and debugging in large-scale applications by providing static type checking, better code organization, and enhanced IDE support.",
        "keyPoints": [
            "Detects errors at compile-time instead of runtime.",
            "Enhances code maintainability with type annotations.",
            "Improves readability and collaboration in large teams.",
            "Provides better tooling support with autocompletion and refactoring."
        ],
